IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `npa-types`
IMPORT `npa-act`

-- INDEPENDENT TESTS — Notaries Public Act 1959. Expected values were decided
-- from the source alone; see independent-expectations.md. A failing
-- assertion is a finding and is left failing.

§ `Independent tests — Notaries Public Act 1959`

GIVEN prac IS A BOOLEAN, yrs IS A NUMBER, fit IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Lawyer
`indep lawyer` prac yrs fit MEANS Lawyer WITH `name` IS "L", `a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore` IS prac, `years practised as an advocate and solicitor in Singapore` IS yrs, `found by the Senate to be fit and proper` IS fit


GIVEN who IS A STRING, k IS A `Kind of appointment`, start IS A DATE, months IS A NUMBER, r5 IS A MAYBE DATE, r6 IS A MAYBE DATE, ret IS A MAYBE DATE, died IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH AN Appointment
`indep appt` who k start months r5 r6 ret died MEANS Appointment WITH `appointee` IS who, `kind` IS k, `takes effect on` IS start, `period in months` IS months, `Council of the Law Society consulted` IS TRUE, `published in the Gazette` IS TRUE, `revoked under s 5 on` IS r5, `revoked under s 6 on` IS r6, `the absent notary returned on` IS ret, `the absent notary died on` IS died

`regular` MEANS `an appointment under s 3(1)`
`temp` MEANS `a temporary appointment under s 3(5)` "N"

`A plain` MEANS `indep appt` "A" `regular` (YMD 2025 7 1) 12 NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING
`A revoked s5` MEANS `indep appt` "A" `regular` (YMD 2025 7 1) 12 (JUST (YMD 2025 10 1)) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING
`A revoked s6` MEANS `indep appt` "A" `regular` (YMD 2025 7 1) 12 NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2025 10 1)) NOTHING NOTHING
`T plain` MEANS `indep appt` "T" `temp` (YMD 2025 7 1) 12 NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING
`T returned` MEANS `indep appt` "T" `temp` (YMD 2025 7 1) 12 NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2025 9 1)) NOTHING
`T died` MEANS `indep appt` "T" `temp` (YMD 2025 7 1) 12 NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2025 9 1))
`T 13 months` MEANS `indep appt` "T" `temp` (YMD 2025 7 1) 13 NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING
`old appt` MEANS `indep appt` "A" `regular` (YMD 2007 1 1) 12 NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING

GIVEN p IS A `Purpose of the affidavit`, inSG IS A BOOLEAN, outSG IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Affidavit
`aff` p inSG outSG MEANS Affidavit WITH `purpose` IS p, `to be used in a court or place within Singapore` IS inSG, `to be used in a court or place outside Singapore` IS outSG

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Section 5 findings`
`findings` a b c MEANS `Section 5 findings` WITH `has become a bankrupt or made an arrangement with creditors` IS a, `has been struck off the roll of advocates and solicitors` IS b, `guilty of misconduct the Senate thinks renders the person unfit to practise as a notary` IS c

GIVEN o IS AN `Oath power`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`permitted` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `the notary may administer the oath, and take or attest the document` u THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the notary may not, under s 4(2)` THEN FALSE

GIVEN dec IS AN `Appointment decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`may appoint` dec MEANS
    CONSIDER dec
    WHEN `the Senate may appoint, in its absolute discretion, and there is no appeal` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 3(1)-(4) — appointment`

#ASSERT `may appoint` (`the s 3(1) decision on` (`indep lawyer` TRUE 7 TRUE) `for` 12 `months, the Council consulted:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `may appoint` (`the s 3(1) decision on` (`indep lawyer` TRUE 6.99 TRUE) `for` 12 `months, the Council consulted:` TRUE)
#ASSERT `may appoint` (`the s 3(1) decision on` (`indep lawyer` TRUE 15 TRUE) `for` 12 `months, the Council consulted:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `may appoint` (`the s 3(1) decision on` (`indep lawyer` FALSE 20 TRUE) `for` 12 `months, the Council consulted:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `may appoint` (`the s 3(1) decision on` (`indep lawyer` TRUE 10 FALSE) `for` 12 `months, the Council consulted:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `may appoint` (`the s 3(1) decision on` (`indep lawyer` TRUE 10 TRUE) `for` 13 `months, the Council consulted:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `may appoint` (`the s 3(1) decision on` (`indep lawyer` TRUE 10 TRUE) `for` 12 `months, the Council consulted:` FALSE)
#ASSERT `qualified under s 3(2):` (`indep lawyer` TRUE 7 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `qualified under s 3(2):` (`indep lawyer` TRUE 6.99 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `qualified under s 3(2):` (`indep lawyer` FALSE 20 TRUE)

§§ `s 3(5)-(6) — temporary appointments`

#ASSERT `the Senate may temporarily appoint` (`indep lawyer` TRUE 2 TRUE) `for an absence from` (YMD 2025 3 1) `to` (YMD 2025 5 1) `, the Council consulted:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Senate may temporarily appoint` (`indep lawyer` TRUE 2 TRUE) `for an absence from` (YMD 2025 3 1) `to` (YMD 2025 4 1) `, the Council consulted:` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Senate may temporarily appoint` (`indep lawyer` TRUE 2 TRUE) `for an absence from` (YMD 2025 3 1) `to` (YMD 2025 4 2) `, the Council consulted:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Senate may temporarily appoint` (`indep lawyer` FALSE 20 TRUE) `for an absence from` (YMD 2025 3 1) `to` (YMD 2025 5 1) `, the Council consulted:` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Senate may temporarily appoint` (`indep lawyer` TRUE 10 TRUE) `for an absence from` (YMD 2007 5 31) `to` (YMD 2007 8 1) `, the Council consulted:` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Senate may temporarily appoint` (`indep lawyer` TRUE 10 TRUE) `for an absence from` (YMD 2007 6 1) `to` (YMD 2007 8 1) `, the Council consulted:` TRUE
#ASSERT `the appointment` `T plain` `has effect on` (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `the appointment` `T plain` `has effect on` (YMD 2026 8 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the appointment` `T 13 months` `has effect on` (YMD 2026 7 15)
#ASSERT `the appointment` `T returned` `has effect on` (YMD 2025 8 31)
#ASSERT NOT `the appointment` `T returned` `has effect on` (YMD 2025 9 2)
#ASSERT NOT `the appointment` `T died` `has effect on` (YMD 2025 9 2)
#ASSERT `the appointment` `A plain` `has effect on` (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `the appointment` `A plain` `has effect on` (YMD 2026 8 1)

§§ `s 2 — who is a notary public`

#ASSERT `a notary public:` "A" `, by the appointments` (LIST `A plain`) `, on` (YMD 2025 9 1)
#ASSERT NOT `a notary public:` "A" `, by the appointments` (LIST `A revoked s5`) `, on` (YMD 2025 11 1)
#ASSERT `a notary public:` "A" `, by the appointments` (LIST `A revoked s5`) `, on` (YMD 2025 9 1)
#ASSERT NOT `a notary public:` "A" `, by the appointments` (LIST `A revoked s6`) `, on` (YMD 2025 11 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `a notary public:` "A" `, by the appointments` (LIST `old appt`) `, on` (YMD 2007 5 31)
#ASSERT `a notary public:` "A" `, by the appointments` (LIST `old appt`) `, on` (YMD 2007 6 1)

§§ `s 4 — oaths and affidavits`

#ASSERT `permitted` (`the s 4 answer for` (`aff` `confirming or proving the due execution of a document` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `permitted` (`the s 4 answer for` (`aff` `executed by the master or a crew member of a vessel about the vessel` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT `permitted` (`the s 4 answer for` (`aff` `another purpose` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `permitted` (`the s 4 answer for` (`aff` `another purpose` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `permitted` (`the s 4 answer for` (`aff` `confirming or proving the due execution of a document` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT REFUSED `the s 4 answer for` (`aff` `another purpose` FALSE FALSE)

§§ `s 5 / s 6 — revocation`

#ASSERT `the Senate must revoke the appointment, on` (`findings` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Senate must revoke the appointment, on` (`findings` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Senate must revoke the appointment, on` (`findings` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the Senate must revoke the appointment, on` (`findings` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Senate must revoke the appointment, on` (`findings` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Senate may revoke under s 6, the notary having requested it:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Senate may revoke under s 6, the notary having requested it:` FALSE

§§ `s 7 — offence`

#ASSERT `s 7 is contravened by` "X" `, by the appointments` (LIST `A plain`) `, on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `, having` TRUE `, within powers:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 7 is contravened by` "A" `, by the appointments` (LIST `A plain`) `, on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `, having` TRUE `, within powers:` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7 is contravened by` "A" `, by the appointments` (LIST `A plain`) `, on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `, having` TRUE `, within powers:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 7 is contravened by` "X" `, by the appointments` (LIST `A plain`) `, on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `, having` FALSE `, within powers:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 7 is contravened by` "T" `, by the appointments` (LIST `T plain`) `, on` (YMD 2025 9 1) `, having` TRUE `, within powers:` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7 is contravened by` "T" `, by the appointments` (LIST `T returned`) `, on` (YMD 2025 9 2) `, having` TRUE `, within powers:` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 7 is contravened by` "X" `, by the appointments` (LIST `A plain`) `, on` (YMD 2007 5 31) `, having` TRUE `, within powers:` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7 is contravened by` "X" `, by the appointments` (LIST `A plain`) `, on` (YMD 2007 6 1) `, having` TRUE `, within powers:` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7 — maximum fine` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT 10000 AT MOST `s 7 — maximum fine`
#ASSERT NOT 10001 AT MOST `s 7 — maximum fine`
#ASSERT `s 7 — the court` EQUALS "on conviction before a District Judge"

§§ `s 8 — rules`

#ASSERT `made within s 8(1):` (Rules WITH `made by the Chief Justice` IS TRUE, `after consulting the Senate` IS TRUE, `published in the Gazette on` IS NOTHING, `later commencement date specified` IS NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `made within s 8(1):` (Rules WITH `made by the Chief Justice` IS TRUE, `after consulting the Senate` IS FALSE, `published in the Gazette on` IS NOTHING, `later commencement date specified` IS NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the day s 8(2) brings into force` (Rules WITH `made by the Chief Justice` IS TRUE, `after consulting the Senate` IS TRUE, `published in the Gazette on` IS JUST (YMD 2025 1 1), `later commencement date specified` IS NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day s 8(2) brings into force` (Rules WITH `made by the Chief Justice` IS TRUE, `after consulting the Senate` IS TRUE, `published in the Gazette on` IS JUST (YMD 2025 1 1), `later commencement date specified` IS JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)
